# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — organized into pattern rules. Sections:
#   1. Python / build / OS
#   2. Secrets & local environment
#   3. Root-level detritus & stray downloads
#   4. data/raw source exclusions (raw downloads; provenance comments verbatim)
#   5. data/clean curated tree (derived, disposable)
#   6. Dashboard / codebase-site generated data
#   7. results/ forecast & scenario caches
#   8. results/calibration slim-bundle rules (heavy regenerable intermediates)
#   9. results/calibration & results/hindcast scratch families
#  10. Misc local caches
# One-off, session-specific scratch-dir names are intentionally NOT enumerated:
# any bundle's heavy contents are already covered by the §8 slim-bundle rules,
# and the recurring scratch families are covered by §9.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Python / build / OS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
dist/
build/
.DS_Store

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Secrets & local environment — never commit credentials. Keys resolve at
#    runtime from a local, untracked .env; commit a keys-only .env.example.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Root-level detritus & stray downloads. Extract archives into data/raw/
#    instead; scratch scripts belong in scripts/probes/, logs are transient.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*.zip
# Stray root-level data dumps belong under data/raw/, never the repo root — this
# is how ~195 MB of *_LMP_GRP_* ERCOT/CAISO archives leaked in (see the clone-bloat
# audit). Generalizes the /*.zip guard above; confirmed no legitimate root-level
# file uses any of these types.
/*.parquet
/*.xlsx
/*.csv
/*.tar.gz
/*.pkl
/*.log
/scratchpad_*.py
/probe_run*.log
/scratch/
/scratchpad/
/scratchpad_logs/
/scratch_hindcast/
/scratch_logs/
/logs/
/logs_g10/
# Local compatibility shim: symlinks (inputs/ -> data/raw/...) so tooling that
# still records the pre-W1-relocation inputs/ paths in old bundle configs can
# resolve them; never a committed artifact.
/inputs/
# Agent tool worktrees (per-session isolated worktrees, not repo content)
.claude/worktrees/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. data/raw source exclusions — raw downloads are re-fetchable and too large
#    for the push endpoint; provenance comments kept verbatim.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-ISO EIA-860 override CSVs — raw source files (parquet/json) are committed
data/raw/eia-860/*.csv

# PJM energy market offers raw monthly parquets — gitignored (large corpus +
# PJM DataMiner2 redistribution terms, see docs/data-licensing.md §4). Refetch/
# curate instructions: data/raw/pjm-energy-offers/README.md.
data/raw/pjm-energy-offers/*
!data/raw/pjm-energy-offers/README.md

# CAISO OASIS DAM public-bid daily zips (~1,096 files / 0.5-0.9 GB for
# 2023-2025): refetch with scripts/fetch_caiso_public_bids.py (see
# data/raw/caiso-public-bids/README.md).
data/raw/caiso-public-bids/*
!data/raw/caiso-public-bids/README.md

# MISO annual bc_HIST source mirrors (~20-70 MB raw each; validation layer
# only, rule 13): refetch with scripts/data/fetch_miso_bc_hist.py (see
# data/raw/transfer-constraint-binding/MISO/README.md provenance table).
data/raw/transfer-constraint-binding/MISO/*_bc_HIST.csv.gz

# PJM DataMiner2 DA virtual-bid feeds (hrl_da_incs_decs, hrl_dmd_bids): same
# non-member redistribution restriction as pjm-energy-offers; refetch with
# scripts/fetch_pjm_da_virtuals.py (see data/raw/pjm-da-virtuals/README.md).
data/raw/pjm-da-virtuals/*
!data/raw/pjm-da-virtuals/README.md

# PJM DataMiner2 transmission-ZONE LMP components (da_hrl_lmps / rt_hrl_lmps,
# type=ZONE): same non-member redistribution restriction; refetch with
# scripts/data/fetch_pjm_zonal_lmp_components.py (see
# data/raw/pjm-zonal-lmp/README.md). Only the dimensionless DERIVED surface
# iso-specific-transmission/PJM_loss_surface.csv is committed. The sha256
# manifest IS committed as the provenance record for that derive.
data/raw/pjm-zonal-lmp/*
!data/raw/pjm-zonal-lmp/README.md
!data/raw/pjm-zonal-lmp/SHA256SUMS.txt

# PJM DataMiner2 day-ahead BINDING TRANSMISSION CONSTRAINTS (da_marginal_value
# / da_transconstraints — monitored facility, contingency, shadow price): same
# non-member redistribution restriction; refetch with
# scripts/data/fetch_pjm_binding_constraints.py (see
# data/raw/pjm-binding-constraints/README.md). The sha256 manifest IS committed
# as the provenance record for the pjm-137 measurement.
data/raw/pjm-binding-constraints/*
!data/raw/pjm-binding-constraints/README.md
!data/raw/pjm-binding-constraints/SHA256SUMS.txt

# PJM DataMiner2 500 kV EHV aggregate-node LMPs (da_hrl_lmps, type=EHV): the
# intra-zonal price-spread measurement. Same non-member redistribution
# restriction; refetch with scripts/data/fetch_pjm_ehv_lmp.py (see
# data/raw/pjm-ehv-lmp/README.md). The sha256 manifest IS committed.
data/raw/pjm-ehv-lmp/*
!data/raw/pjm-ehv-lmp/README.md
!data/raw/pjm-ehv-lmp/SHA256SUMS.txt

# NYISO MIS public DAM zonal LBMP monthly archives (36 zips, ~13 MB): raw
# source of nyiso_proxy_lmp_hourly_NEISO.parquet (committed). Regenerable
# byte-identical from the stable public URLs
# (http://mis.nyiso.com/public/csv/damlbmp/YYYYMM01damlbmp_zone_csv.zip) —
# too large for this remote's push limit, so gitignored like the PJM
# energy-offer corpus above; fetch + rebuild:
# scripts/build_nyiso_proxy_lmp_neiso.py (docstring has the curl loop).
data/raw/lmp-data/NYISO/*damlbmp_zone_csv.zip
data/raw/lmp-data/NYISO/*realtime_zone_csv.zip
# Transient outer container the derive_actual_lmp NYISO DA reader consumes
# (assembled locally from the monthly damlbmp zips above; same re-fetchable
# lineage — the committed actual_lmp_hourly_NYISO.parquet is the durable
# record, per the holdout-register staging precedent).
data/raw/lmp-data/NYISO/NYISO_zonal_hourly.zip

# NYISO ancillary-services raw pull cache.
data/raw/NYISO-AS/raw/
# ISO-NE hourly reserve-requirement window CSVs (75 files, 2023-2025): kept
# out of the pack per the NYISO-archive precedent; regenerate with
# scripts/fetch_neiso_reserve_requirements.py (README.md in that dir).
data/raw/NEISO-AS/requirements/requirements_*.csv
# ISO-NE DA energy-offer daily CSVs (~1.4 GB for 2023-2025): gitignored, same
# precedent; regenerate with scripts/fetch_neiso_da_energy_offers.py.
data/raw/NEISO-AS/da-energy-offers/hbdayaheadenergyoffer_*.csv
# ISO-NE DA demand-bid daily CSVs (~2.3 MB/day, ~2.5 GB for the full 2023-2025
# corpus) + the DA cleared-demand window files: same precedent; regenerate with
# scripts/data/fetch_neiso_da_demand_bids.py (full corpus) or
# scripts/probes/_neiso76_demand_limb.py --fetch (the 41-day Phase-0 sample).
data/raw/NEISO-AS/da-demand-bids/hbdayaheaddemandbid_*.csv
data/raw/NEISO-AS/da-demand-bids/cleared_*.csv
# ISO-NE DA SUBMITTED import-offer / export-bid daily CSVs (~0.35 MB/day,
# ~380 MB for 2023-2025): same precedent; regenerate with
# scripts/data/fetch_neiso_da_import_export.py (README.md in that dir).
data/raw/NEISO-AS/da-import-export/hbdayaheadimpexp_*.csv
# ISO-NE reserve CLEARING-PRICE window CSVs (RT final RZPD + DAAS day-ahead):
# validation-only measured prices, same precedent; regenerate with
# scripts/probes/_neiso76_reserve_content.py --fetch (README.md in that dir).
data/raw/NEISO-AS/reserve-prices/rzpd_final_*.csv
data/raw/NEISO-AS/reserve-prices/daas_*.csv
# ISO-NE Morning Report daily CSVs (~2,940 files, 2018-07 -> present): gitignored,
# same precedent; the committed neiso_operable_capacity_daily.csv is the
# deliverable. Regenerate with scripts/data/fetch_neiso_morning_report.py, then
# scripts/data/build_neiso_operable_capacity.py (README.md in that dir).
data/raw/neiso-operable-capacity/daily/morning_report_*.csv

# NOAA GHCN-Daily raw per-station pull cache for scripts/fetch_zone_temperature.py
# (re-fetchable; --no-fetch re-derives the zone CSVs from it). NEVER commit — the
# raw station archives are hundreds of MB and trip the remote's 413 push limit.
data/raw/*-weather/_ghcn_cache/

# Derived binned-fleet cache (side output of the fleet loader)
data/raw/_processed-legacy/*.parquet
# The EIA-923 extracts ARE committed: they are small (~16 KB cost,
# ~225 KB generation) and produced once by
# scripts/process_f923_fuel_costs.py; the dispatch fuel resolver and
# the calibration diagnostic read them at runtime.
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/eia923_monthly_fuel_costs.parquet
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/eia923_monthly_generation.parquet
# Derived CAMPD reference artifacts — per-plant parasitic-load factors and
# emission rates, read at runtime by the dispatch LP and calibration report.
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/parasitic_load_factors.parquet
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/plant_emission_rates.parquet
# fossil_co2_rates is likewise committed (fast-path fleet-wide CO2 rates read by
# market_sim.data.egrid). It was tracked before this allowlist existed, so it
# stayed tracked-but-ignored; naming it here keeps a fresh copy `git add`-able.
# The un-negated case is what silently stranded the 2026-07-04 F5 rows of
# plant_emission_rates.parquet — see docs/iso-2022-holdout-data-availability-audit-2026-07.md §5.2.
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/fossil_co2_rates.parquet
# Per-year EIA-860 plant-level CHP flag lookup (~0.5 MB), produced by
# scripts/build_eia860_chp_by_year.py from the committed EIA-860 release zips.
# The fleet loader reads it so a multi-year backcast buckets each year's gas
# cogens with that year's CHP designation instead of the latest snapshot's.
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/eia860_chp_by_year.parquet
# Class-totals cache for scripts/derive_offer_curve_jacobian.py (rebuilt on
# demand from the calibration bundles; the CSV it derives IS committed)
data/raw/_processed-legacy/.offer_curve_jacobian_cache.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. data/clean curated tree is DERIVED and disposable: regenerated from
#    data/raw by the per-datatype scripts/curate_*.py (each writing through
#    scripts/lib/clean_io.write_clean). Sessions commit the curation script + its
#    test, never the generated parquet. The schema YAMLs and the data dictionary
#    under data/dictionary/ ARE committed (they are the contract, not output).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data/clean/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Dashboard / codebase-site generated data. frontend/data/backcast/*.js
#    (manifest/benchmark/completeness) ARE committed (raw-checkout preview via
#    the bc-data.js fallback); the "Deploy site to GitHub Pages" workflow is
#    their single writer on main. The codebase-site subset below is generated at
#    deploy time by scripts/build_codebase_site_backcast.py and never committed.
#    The RETIRED keeper/status monoliths (sharded per-ISO 2026-07-19 into
#    keepers/<ISO>.json + status/<ISO>.js so parallel promotions never collide)
#    are ignored so a stale tool can't resurrect them into a commit.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/codebase-site/data/backcast/
frontend/data/backcast/keepers.json
frontend/data/backcast/status.js

# Forecast dashboard (FF-5A) generated data. The registry/runs/manifest/
# program-status.js under frontend/data/forecast/ are DERIVED from the committed
# inputs (frontend/data/hindcast/*.json + ff-verdicts.json + program-status.json)
# and regenerated by the Pages deploy (register_forecast_run.py --reindex, its
# single writer). Regenerate locally with the same command for the file://
# preview. The committed inputs (program-status.json, ff-verdicts.json) are NOT
# ignored — they are the source, not output.
frontend/data/forecast/registry/
frontend/data/forecast/runs/
frontend/data/forecast/manifest.js
frontend/data/forecast/program-status.js

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. results/ forecast & scenario caches — transient per-ISO LP outputs keyed by
#    cache_key (results/<ISO>/<cache_key>/). Only results/calibration/ bundles
#    are tracked; capacity-expansion forecast runs are reproducible from config.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/results/ERCOT/
/results/CAISO/
/results/PJM/
/results/MISO/
/results/NYISO/
/results/NEISO/
# Full-horizon forecast runs and ad-hoc forecast probes: disposable diagnostic
# cache, never committed (forecast probes are not dashboard-registered —
# CLAUDE.md rule 15/16; regenerate from config). Covers the run dirs and their
# loose top-level run logs (e.g. results/probe-pjm-rps.log).
/results/full-horizon/
/results/ff-t1f-baseline/
# D-9 forecast warm-start A/B arms (scripts/probes/_d9_forecast_warmstart_ab.py
# --out-dir). Same class as /results/full-horizon/ — it IS a full-horizon
# forecast solve, one per arm, and nothing here is dashboard-registered. The
# measured readout lives in docs/handoffs/wallclock-baseline-2026-07.md.
/results/d9-ab/
/results/probe-*/
/results/verify-*/
# FFR-1A confirmed-exit accounting acceptance probes (isolated run_full_horizon
# --out-dir caches + logs). Same class as /results/full-horizon/.
/results/ffr1a/
# FFR-2C net-CONE re-anchor before/after T0 smoke (NEISO 2026-2028, isolated
# run_full_horizon --out-dir caches). Same class as /results/ffr1a/ — a T0
# regression probe, not dashboard-registered. The measured readout (identical
# cache key, content-identical year parquets, unchanged invariants) lives in
# docs/handoffs/ffr-2c-net-cone-currency-2026-08-02.md §6; the paired
# capacity-price validation JSONs it cites ARE committed, under
# results/capacity-price-validation/.
/results/ffr2c/
# FFR-2E shipped-vs-fixed capacity-price posture T0 arms (PJM 2026-2028,
# isolated run_full_horizon --out-dir caches). Same class as /results/ffr2c/ —
# the committed record is the registered sidecar under
# frontend/data/hindcast/, and the readout lives in
# docs/handoffs/ffr-2e-shipped-capacity-posture-2026-08-02.md §4.
/results/ffr2e/
/results/*.log
# Backcast diagnostic-probe solve output (scripts/probes/* --out-dir default,
# e.g. results/probes/pjm119_eastcut). Same class as the /results/probe-*/ rule
# above: a probe is never dashboard-registered (CLAUDE.md rule 15/16 — a
# single-year solve may not be a keeper), and the bundles carry the heavy
# regenerable LP intermediates the slim-bundle rules exclude anyway
# (dispatch/<year>_P1.parquet alone is ~80 MB and would trip the remote's 413
# push limit). Regenerate with scripts/replay_keeper.py --out-dir; the measured
# readouts live in the finding docs.
/results/probes/
# warm-start solver benchmark output + captured-LP cache (generated by
# scripts/bench_warmstart.py / bench_warmstart_xyear.py; measured numbers live
# in docs/cross-year-warmstart.md).
/results/warmstart_bench.txt
/results/warmstart_xyear_bench.txt
/results/warmstart_xyear_capture.pkl
# Cold-solve bench captures: the real pickled ISO-year LP (fleet, demand,
# build kwargs, mc vectors) written by scripts/archive/bench_cold_solve.py
# `capture` and read by scripts/diagnostics/bench_highs_parallel.py. Hundreds
# of MB each (ERCOT 2023 425 MB, MISO 2024 co-opt 817 MB) — regenerable from
# the capture command, and they would trip the remote's 413 push limit. The
# measured verdicts live in docs/handoffs/wallclock-baseline-2026-07.md.
/results/bench_capture_*.pkl
/results/bench-parallel/
# Persisted year-1 cross-year warm-start basis cache (plan §7 H2). Disposable
# NPZ, schema-keyed, delete-and-recapture on mismatch (never committed);
# regenerated by any calibration solve with MARKET_SIM_WARMSTART_XYEAR set.
/results/basis-cache/
# Outage-gate audit scratch.
/results/outage_gate_audit/
# Stage-0 regression goldens (docs/handoffs/orchestrator-unification-plan-2026-07.md
# §7.3): multi-GB re-solved keeper bundles used only for before/after stage
# comparison. The bundles live in <stage-tag>/<ISO>/ subdirs — ignore those (they
# trip the remote's 413 push limit); the hashes-only <stage-tag>/manifest.json
# stays tracked as the committed deliverable.
/results/regression-goldens/*/*/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. results/calibration slim-bundle rules. Bundles are committed slim: only the
#    text files (meta/run_config/metrics/legitimacy_diagnostics/attestation/
#    SUMMARY) + the dashboard payload. The per-hour dispatch dir, system/storage/
#    btm/scarcity/availability/posture/flows parquets, floors, solve logs and the
#    captured model_changes.diff are large regenerable intermediates. Rules cover
#    both the flat (results/calibration/<name>/) and ISO-scoped
#    (results/calibration/<ISO>/<name>/) bundle layouts.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/calibration/*/model_changes.diff
results/calibration/*/dispatch/
results/calibration/*/*.parquet
results/calibration/*/floors/
# Per-unit / per-link hourly sidecars — excluded BY DEFAULT; bundles normally
# commit only hourly/{class_hourly,storage,system,reserve_family} (rule 15).
#
# The two grounds this exclusion used to state ("~58 MB/bundle", "regenerable by
# a replay") were both MEASURED FALSE at nyiso-116 (2026-08-03) and are corrected
# here rather than left to mislead:
#   * SIZE — NYISO measures 920 KB/yr (unit) + 170 KB/yr (network) = 3.2 MB for a
#     whole 3-year bundle. The ~58 MB figure predates the DELTA_BINARY_PACKED
#     ``hour`` encoding (see _write_hourly_sidecar's docstring: CAISO's unit frame
#     went 12.60 MB -> 1.74 MB from that change alone).
#   * REPLAY — nyiso-114 §2 measured that a keeper arming a P0-run-pattern bridge
#     CANNOT be re-solved into byte-identity once main has moved (caiso-155 vertex
#     dependence), so for such a keeper this layer is PERMANENTLY unrecoverable.
#
# So the default stays (these are still the bundle's largest frames and most
# bundles are never interrogated at unit grain), but a lane that WILL interrogate
# a bundle commits its layer deliberately with ``git add -f`` — see the
# unit_network_layer_sidecar matrix row. Opt-in per bundle, not a policy flip.
results/calibration/*/hourly/unit_hourly_*.parquet
results/calibration/*/hourly/network_*.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/hourly/unit_hourly_*.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/hourly/network_*.parquet
results/calibration/*/solve.log
results/calibration/*-capdel-probe.log
results/calibration/*/_shared/
results/calibration/_shared/
results/calibration/logs/
# ISO-scoped (two-level) bundle internals — the single-* rules above miss them.
results/calibration/*/*/model_changes.diff
results/calibration/*/*/dispatch/
results/calibration/*/*/floors/
results/calibration/*/*/system.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/storage.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/btm.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/availability_rcpf*.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/scarcity*.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/posture.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/flows.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/solve.log
results/calibration/*/*/_shared/

# Probe-local CLEAN trees. The offer-surface probes curate into their own clean
# root under results/calibration/ (the `--clean-root` default of
# _caiso152_rle_parse_bias.py and _caiso153_offer_classifier_reid.py), which is
# DERIVED, disposable data in the sense of the data/clean/ contract — ~234 MB
# for the CAISO 2023-25 dam-public-bids span, regenerable by re-running
# `curate`. It is never an input to a committed result and must never enter a
# pack (the remote rejects large packs with HTTP 413).
results/calibration/clean_*/
results/calibration/*/clean_*/

# Session-local CLEAN staging. A partition-restoration A/B (caiso-157) has to
# move curated partitions in and out of data/clean around each arm so each arm
# solves the input state it declares; the holding area is the same DERIVED,
# disposable data as data/clean itself and is regenerable by re-running the
# curate scripts. Never an input to a committed result.
.clean_stash/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. results/calibration & results/hindcast scratch families — recurring
#    throwaway-probe naming (rule 14/16: never registered keepers; regenerable
#    from run_config.json). One-off per-session dir names are NOT enumerated;
#    their heavy contents are already ignored by §8.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/calibration/*probe*/
results/calibration/_diag_*
results/calibration/caiso_diag_*/
results/calibration/miso_diag_*
results/calibration/*_repro_A/
# Rule-12 per-year chain scaffolding. A multi-year per-plant solve is chained
# one FRESH year per process (scripts/probes/_<session>_chain.sh: miso-109,
# miso-111, pjm-143 …), where each intermediate link `<bundle>_y<NN>` byte-
# copies the earlier years forward via --reuse-solved and the FINAL link is the
# bundle. The intermediates are duplicate partial bundles that the chain script
# deletes on completion — never a deliverable, and never to be committed if a
# chain dies before its own cleanup.
results/calibration/*_y2[0-9]/
# caiso-122 attribution arms: the same-HEAD control (no delta), its single-year
# leg, and the keeper-era counterfactual (outage extract hidden). All three are
# repro/control arms under the FINDING-caiso92b protocol — never registered,
# never committed; only the registered delta bundle is a deliverable.
results/calibration/caiso122_control_A/
results/calibration/caiso122_headctl_2025/
results/calibration/caiso122_nooutage_2025/
# ercot-130 Phase 1 availability cache: the keeper's coal availability array
# captured from the live fleet-array path (no LP). Derived and disposable —
# regenerate with `scripts/probes/ercot130_capoff_phase1.py --capture`.
results/calibration/_ercot130_avail_cache/
# miso-98 CHP-sector A/B staging legs. MISO peaks at 14.4 GB on a 15 GB box
# (miso-92 §7), so each three-year bundle is built one fresh year per process
# and chained forward with --reuse-solved. Only the two FINAL three-year
# bundles (miso98_chp_sector_A / _B) are deliverables; these legs are
# regenerable from their own run_config.json and must never be registered —
# a single-year bundle is not a keeper (rule 16 [R-ALLYEARS]).
results/calibration/miso98_chp_sector_A_y23/
results/calibration/miso98_chp_sector_A_y2324/
results/calibration/miso98_chp_sector_B_y23/
results/calibration/miso98_chp_sector_B_y2324/
# miso-106 measured-CT-heat-rate A/B staging legs — same OOM, same remedy. A
# first attempt at all three years in ONE process was OOM-killed on 2025 at
# 15.9 GB anon-rss, so both arms are rebuilt one fresh year per process and
# chained forward with --reuse-solved. Only the two FINAL three-year bundles
# (miso106_control_A / miso106_ctheatrate_B) are deliverables; these legs are
# regenerable from their own run_config.json and must never be registered —
# a single-year bundle is not a keeper (rule 16 [R-ALLYEARS]).
results/calibration/_armA_y23/
results/calibration/_armA_y2324/
results/calibration/_armB_y23/
results/calibration/_armB_y2324/
# miso-96 staged --reuse-solved chain legs: the 15 GB box OOMs a 3-year
# single-process MISO solve (14.34 GB single-year peak), so the arm is built one
# fresh year per process and each leg byte-copies the prior years forward. Only
# the final full-span bundle (results/calibration/miso96_sunkfixed/) is a
# deliverable and gets registered (rule 16 [R-ALLYEARS] — one bundle, all three
# years); the legs are scaffolding, regenerable from their run_config.json.
results/calibration/miso96_sunkfixed_y23/
results/calibration/miso96_sunkfixed_y2324/
results/calibration/caiso122_prelayup_2025/
results/calibration/caiso106_binding_*/
results/calibration/*_y20[0-9][0-9]/
# Per-year probe accumulator scaffolding (e.g. results/calibration/_miso70_acc/
# {main,base}/y2023): fully disposable intermediates — the registered final
# bundles are the deliverable.
results/calibration/_*_acc/
results/calibration/MISO/_diag_*
results/calibration/MISO/_repro_logs/
# Capacity-hindcast bundle internals are reproducible from the recorded config;
# the committed deliverable is the slim set (meta.json + score.json + frontend
# sidecar + report). Ledgers/configs committed under the earlier convention stay
# tracked (gitignore never untracks).
results/hindcast/*/*/*/year_*.parquet
results/hindcast/*/*/*/evolution_*.json
results/hindcast/*/*/*/year_*_floor_retentions.json
results/hindcast/*/*/*/config.yaml
results/hindcast/*/*/*/*.parquet
results/hindcast/*/run_config.yaml
results/hindcast/*.log
results/hindcast/*/run.log

# FF-2B base-year adequacy solves (results/ff2b-after/<iso>, run via
# run_full_horizon at T0 scale for the 2026 I7 check the *-ff-2b-adequacy
# sidecars point to): the slim deliverable is full_horizon_summary.json +
# evolution_*.json (the capacity accounting); the dispatch parquet and config
# are reproducible from the recorded run. The ff2b-before/ baselines are
# unreferenced diagnostic scratch (disposable, no sidecar points at them).
/results/ff2b-before/
results/ff2b-after/*/*/*/year_*.parquet
results/ff2b-after/*/*/*/config.yaml

# FFR-1C base-year hydro-accreditation A/B (results/ffr1c/{before,after}-<iso>,
# run_full_horizon at T0 scale for the 2026 I7 probe both arms' forecast-namespace
# sidecars point to). Same class as the ff2b-* solves above: the slim deliverable
# is full_horizon_summary.json + evolution_*.json (the capacity accounting the I7
# numbers are read from); the dispatch parquet, config and run log are
# reproducible from the recorded run. BOTH arms are kept here (unlike ff2b) —
# the before-arm is the A/B control a sidecar does point at.
results/ffr1c/*/*/*/year_*.parquet
results/ffr1c/*/*/*/config.yaml
results/ffr1c/*.log

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. Misc local caches (docs/handoffs driver scratch — the committed
#     deliverables are the driver-battery-<iso>-<date>.{md,json} memos).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/handoffs/_fom_grid_cache/
docs/handoffs/_foresight_ab_cache/
docs/handoffs/_battery_cache_*/
docs/handoffs/_battery_metrics/

# FF-3B CES T1-scale POC: disposable per-year solve cache + logs, and the
# throwaway driver/registration instrumentation. The committed POC deliverables
# are docs/handoffs/ff-3b-ces-poc-2026-07.md (with the wall/RSS ledger + report
# tables) and the kind="ces-poc" sidecars under frontend/data/hindcast/ (which
# carry meta.per_year_perf for FF-3E).
/results/ces-poc/
/scratchpad-local/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 11. Push-staging scaffolding & stray probes (repo-clone-bloat-fix 2026-07).
#     One-off relay workarounds and scratch binaries must never re-enter the
#     pack — they are the "manual upload / push-scaffolding" clutter that bloats
#     the clone. Move real work onto its real path and push the bytes directly;
#     never commit a base64-chunked archive or a *_push_staging/ tarball again.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
scripts/_rule27_push_staging/
**/_*_push_staging/
**/_push_staging/
*.tar.gz.b64.part*.txt
# Stray binary / scratch probes dropped at the repo root or in-tree.
/tmp_bin_probe.bin
/*.bin
tmp_*.bin
*_probe.bin

# caiso-122 session solve logs (transient; the finding + bundle are the deliverable).
/scratch_logs/
.comp_cache/
results/calibration/caiso154_slopes_PJM.csv

# FFR-3A owner-decision execution + T1 re-gate battery (run_full_horizon /
# run_capacity_hindcast --out-dir caches and their loose run logs). Same class
# as /results/ffr1a/ and /results/full-horizon/ — forecast legs are registered
# to frontend/data/forecast/ via scripts/register_forecast_run.py, never as
# tracked bundles here (CLAUDE.md rule 15). results/ffr3a/README.md stays
# TRACKED (it is the lane's record, not an output) and is unaffected by this
# rule, which only ever applies to untracked paths.
/results/ffr3a/

# FFR-3C collapse-attribution lane (run_full_horizon --out-dir caches and their
# loose run logs for the paired MISO arms). Same class as /results/ffr3a/ and
# /results/full-horizon/ — forecast legs are registered to
# frontend/data/forecast/ via scripts/register_forecast_run.py, never as tracked
# bundles here (CLAUDE.md rule 15). results/ffr3c/README.md stays TRACKED (it is
# the lane's record, not an output) and is unaffected by this rule, which only
# ever applies to untracked paths.
/results/ffr3c/

# FFR-3A-2 consolidated T1 battery close (run_full_horizon / run_capacity_hindcast
# / run_driver_battery --out-dir caches and their loose run logs). Same class as
# /results/ffr3a/ and /results/ffr3c/ — forecast legs are registered to
# frontend/data/forecast/ via scripts/register_forecast_run.py, never as tracked
# bundles here (CLAUDE.md rule 15). results/ffr3a2/README.md stays TRACKED (it is
# the lane's record, not an output) and is unaffected by this rule, which only
# ever applies to untracked paths.
/results/ffr3a2/

# Transient CT-artifact stash written by scripts/probes/caiso160_nyiso_ct_arms.py
# while a control arm solves against a prior artifact revision; the driver
# restores the working copy and removes this in a finally.
.caiso160_artifact_stash_*/
